# r05 OVER-REJECTION - O17 (D15): a value local declared with ":=" from a call whose result holds references borrowed
# from an argument cannot be lent even to a READ-ONLY receiver: "toks := split(line); toks.Len()" is O17, "the callee
# can store through it" - List.Len cannot. The same value declared with its type, "toks List<String&> = split(line)",
# compiles, as do split(line).Len() and a list filled in place. Hit at once by a tokenizer returning its tokens.
#
# expected: 1
# actual: error[O17] at line 16 "this value's references live where its own storage does not, and the callee can store
#         through it - declare it a reference where they live ('x T&y = ...')"
fn split(line String&) List<String&> {
    toks := List<String&>()
    toks.Push(line[0:1])
    return toks
}
fn count(line String&) I64 {
    toks := split(line)
    return toks.Len()
}
fn main() ? {
    println($count("ab"))
}
